      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T03:24:09Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(3d): 3D Adaptive gets a Method choice with a Trochoidal method per level\n\n3D Pocket has a new parameter `method` (Spiral or Trochoidal), read\nonly under the Adaptive strategy. Spiral is the default: the path and\nthe stamp of every earlier 3D Adaptive are what they were.\n\nUnder Trochoidal each level of the plain ladder is cleared by the 2D\nAdaptive lane planner on the level's own cutter-centre area\n(`machining2d::adaptive_troch_level`, `machining3d::troch`). The posted\nlevel is checked against the level area and the crossing law. A bore\nstarts on a plane only where the run proved its helix disc cleared, else\nover the stock top. A level the method cannot cut is cut by the Spiral\nplan and said with its Z. The rest pass, the offset shells and the\nrotary wrap keep the plan they had.\n\nThe choice is on the Passes tab (Adaptive only), in the project file\n(`method`, absent reads as spiral), in the stamp (Adaptive with\nTrochoidal only) and in the MCP params patch.\n\nStacked on #2149 (same function `ladder`).\n\nFixes #1591\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
